<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sakarya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Sakarya · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922">Greco-Turkish War (1919–1922)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sakarya was fought from 23 August to 13 September 1921 along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakarya-river">Sakarya River</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922">Greco-Turkish War</a>. The Turkish nationalist army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a> halted the Greek advance on Ankara after three weeks of fighting, forcing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> to withdraw. It was the turning point of the war, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a> awarded Mustafa Kemal the title Gazi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sakarya.jpg" alt="Battle of Sakarya" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sfisek · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Sakarya_1921.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
